{"benchmark": "ifeval", "task_id": "1092", "sample_idx": 38, "model_name": "nvidia/nemotron-3-super-120b-a12b", "content": "**Cherry Blossoms and City Lights: My Japan Adventure**\n\nLanding in Tokyo felt like stepping into a living postcard. Neon signs flickered over Shibuya Crossing while the scent of freshly grilled yakitori drifted from tiny alley stalls. I spent my first morning wandering the serene Meiji Shrine, where towering cedars whispered centuries of tradition, then lost myself in the electric buzz of Akihabara’s gaming arcades.\n\nA bullet train whisked me west to Kyoto, where time seemed to slow. I rented a bicycle and pedaled through the Philosopher’s Path, flanked by pink sakura petals that floated like confetti. The golden pavilion of Kinkaku‑ji shimmered against a mirror‑still pond, and I joined locals in a quiet tea ceremony, savoring matcha’s earthy depth.\n\nNo trip to Japan is complete without Osaka’s culinary playground. I dove into steaming bowls of ramen in Dotonbori, laughed with street vendors over takoyaki, and ended each night with a view of the illuminated Glico Man sign, feeling the city’s playful heartbeat.\n\nBetween temples, trains, and tasty bites, Japan offered a perfect blend of ancient grace and futuristic zest. I left with a suitcase full of souvenirs, a camera roll bursting with color, and a promise to return—because one visit is never enough to capture all its wonder.", "logprobs": [{"token": "We", "logprob": -0.11879437416791916}, {"token": " need", "logprob": -0.0031175841577351093}, {"token": " to", "logprob": -0.08381152153015137}, {"token": " write", "logprob": -0.616640031337738}, {"token": " a", "logprob": -0.01833830215036869}, {"token": " short", "logprob": -0.0005654881824739277}, {"token": " blog", "logprob": -2.861018856492592e-06}, {"token": " post", "logprob": -7.676783570786938e-05}, {"token": " about", "logprob": -0.10214941948652267}, {"token": " a", "logprob": -0.00012790338951162994}, {"token": " trip", "lo